msgid ""
msgstr ""
"# Accuracy Comparison Example\n"
"\n"
"This document provides a detailed comparison of the accuracy of different translation methods through specific examples, aiming to help users understand the advantages and applicable scenarios of each method.\n"
"\n"
"## Example 1: Simple Sentence Translation\n"
"\n"
"**Original text:** The weather is nice today.\n"
"\n"
"| Translation Method | Translation Result | Accuracy Assessment |\n"
"|-------------------|-------------------|---------------------|\n"
"| Rule-based Method | Today's weather is very good. | 90% - Semantics are correct, but word order is slightly unnatural |\n"
"| Statistical Method | Today's weather is not bad. | 85% - Semantics are correct, but tone is slightly off |\n"
"| Neural Network Method | The weather is really nice today. | 98% - Semantics and tone are both accurate |\n"
"\n"
"## Example 2: Complex Sentence Translation\n"
"\n"
"**Original text:** Despite the heavy rain, the construction team managed to complete the project ahead of schedule.\n"
"\n"
"| Translation Method | Translation Result | Accuracy Assessment |\n"
"|-------------------|-------------------|---------------------|\n"
"| Rule-based Method | Despite the heavy rain, the construction team still managed to complete the project ahead of schedule. | 85% - Semantics are correct, but sentence structure is slightly rigid |\n"
"| Statistical Method | Although it rained heavily, the construction team still completed the project ahead of schedule. | 90% - Semantics are correct, but some details are missing |\n"
"| Neural Network Method | Despite the heavy rain, the construction team successfully completed the project ahead of schedule. | 97% - Semantics are complete, and the expression is natural |\n"
"\n"
"## Example 3: Translation of Idioms\n"
"\n"
"**Original text:** 他这个人总是画蛇添足。\n"
"\n"
"| Translation Method | Translation Result | Accuracy Assessment |\n"
"|-------------------|-------------------|---------------------|\n"
"| Rule-based Method | He always draws a snake and adds feet. | 40% - Literal translation, failing to convey the meaning of the idiom |\n"
"| Statistical Method | He always adds unnecessary details. | 75% - Semantics are roughly correct, but the cultural connotation is lost |\n"
"| Neural Network Method | He always gilds the lily. | 95% - Both the semantics and cultural connotation are accurately conveyed |\n"
"\n"
"## Example 4: Translation of Technical Documents\n"
"\n"
"**Original text:** The API endpoint requires authentication via OAuth 2.0 protocol.\n"
"\n"
"| Translation Method | Translation Result | Accuracy Assessment |\n"
"|-------------------|-------------------|---------------------|\n"
"| Rule-based Method | The API endpoint requires authentication through the OAuth 2.0 protocol. | 92% - Technical terms are accurate, but the sentence structure is slightly rigid |\n"
"| Statistical Method | The API endpoint requires authentication using the OAuth 2.0 protocol. | 90% - Technical terms are accurate, but the expression is slightly awkward |\n"
"| Neural Network Method | The API endpoint requires authentication via the OAuth 2.0 protocol. | 98% - Technical terms are accurate, and the expression is natural |\n"
"\n"
"## Summary\n"
"\n"
"From the above examples, it can be seen that:\n"
"\n"
"1. **Neural Network Method** performs best in most cases, especially when handling complex sentences, idioms, and technical documents.\n"
"2. **Rule-based Method** performs well in simple sentence translation but is less effective with complex structures and idioms.\n"
"3. **Statistical Method** falls between the two, but may lose some details or cultural connotations.\n"
"\n"
"It is recommended to choose the appropriate translation method based on specific needs. For high-precision requirements, the neural network method is preferred.\n"

